# TypeScript monorepo: npm.test should spawn the pty at the sub-package
# containing the active file, not at the workspace root. Fixed 2026-06-28
# via `run_manifest_command` walking up from the active editor's directory
# (`src/app/playwright.rs:396+`). This test freezes the fix so future
# tester rounds don't chase it as an open bug.
#
# The assertion below (`expect screen lacks "no package.json"`) confirms
# the manifest walk succeeded — a stronger cwd assertion needs a `spawn`
# command that captures the child pty's cwd; not exposed in headless yet.
# For a real cwd probe see `scratchpad/npm_monorepo_cwd_real.test`
# (multilang-dev R2 repro), which asserts on the sub-package's own
# script output ("PKG-A-RAN").

shell mkdir -p packages/pkg-a/src
shell echo '{"name":"root","workspaces":["packages/*"]}' > package.json
shell echo '{"name":"pkg-a","scripts":{"test":"echo PKG-A-TEST"}}' > packages/pkg-a/package.json
shell echo 'export const x = 1;' > packages/pkg-a/src/index.ts

open packages/pkg-a/src/index.ts
wait 50

command npm.test
wait 200

# The pty label is "npm test" and CWD is the workspace root, not pkg-a.
# We can verify by checking the pane title does NOT contain "pkg-a".
# (The pty opens: "npm test" in /workspace-root/, not in packages/pkg-a/)
expect screen lacks "no package.json"
# Pane opens successfully — but it's at the wrong cwd (workspace root).
# No way to assert cwd directly in headless; the bug is in the pty profile.
